 "about_text": "The Box is a Los Angeles gallery founded in 2007 by Mara McCarthy, in conversation with her father, the artist Paul McCarthy. It first opened on Chung King Road in Chinatown before relocating in 2012 to the Arts District of Downtown Los Angeles. The gallery built its program around historically overlooked and forgotten artists, particularly those working in performance, feminist, and radical political practices, including figures such as Barbara T. Smith, Simone Forti, Stan VanDerBeek, and Wally Hedrick. Over time the program expanded to include dance, painting, music and sound, sculpture, social justice projects, performance, and gallery editions, positioning itself as an artist-centered space engaging the commercial art market on its own terms. The Box announced its closing in April 2026 after nineteen years of operation.",
