  "site_notes": "The Box organizes its site around a single 'artists' roster index, an 'about' page, and a large flat collection of individual exhibition pages under /exhibitions-events (current/upcoming) and /exhibitions-events-2 (an older, now largely superseded listing); there is no separate archive-by-year list, so each past show's own page serves as the archive record, though many of these (indices 47,59,101-119) are near-empty stub pages with no usable content. No dedicated news, fairs, or contact/hours pages appear in the inventory. The Box's site is organized around a single 'exhibitions-events' CMS collection: individual exhibition pages (each a discrete show), plus auto-generated per-artist 'category' and 'tag' listing pages that aggregate an artist's exhibition history rather than serve as bios; a separate paginated 'artists' collection (with cursor offsets) functions as the roster index. No standalone about, current-exhibitions landing, or contact page appears in this slice of the inventory, so likely top-level nav pages are missing and were added to fetch_more. The site paginates a single combined exhibitions/events feed via offset query parameters, producing many near-duplicate archiv",
